Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 11:57:01 2026 +0000

    [+208] dsk_rah_fill: the loader's header peek fills to the cylinder's end (kernel hot-paths pass 1)
    
    A package launch peeks the file's first sector for the header, then reads
    the whole file. The peek misses SPEC.md 18.95's cache and FILLS a slot -
    but only to the end of the TRACK, nine sectors at most, so the read behind
    it began a fresh int 13h at the next track, where its own direct path would
    have run on to the end of the cylinder. MEASURED (MartyPC FDC calls, the
    360KB apps disk): Note Pad, TexPad and Paint each took ONE CALL MORE than
    the cylinders they occupy - 8/0/1 x9, 8/1/1 x9, 9/0/1 for Note Pad.
    
    The loader now arms a hint across that one peek - the file's sectors, a
    byte (dsk_rah_hint) - and a fill it causes runs to the bound dsk_xfer's own
    reads use: the cylinder on a two-headed floppy whose FDC was seen to cross a
    head (SPEC.md 18.91.1, [dsk_cylrun]), else the track; and no further than the
    file. When that is more than one slot it is ONE int 13h into the first m
    slots, each record then stamped with its own nine (`.multi`), so every slot
    is still an ordinary single chunk that a later fill evicts alone and no
    record describes storage another owns. More slots than the claim holds,
    and it is the one-slot fill it always was. A span across a 64KB page is
    cut there by dsk_runcap as any read is: two calls, as before, never a wrong
    byte. The hint is disarmed straight after the peek on every path.
    
    Calls per launch (FDC counters, base -> tip):
      360KB   Calc 1 -> 1, Note Pad 3 -> 2, TexPad 3 -> 2, Paint 4 -> 3
      1.44MB  Calc 1 -> 1, Note Pad 2 -> 1, TexPad 2 -> 1, Paint 3 -> 2
    so one int 13h comes off every launch of a package bigger than the slot the
    peek used to fill - ~400 ms each on the 5150 (PERFORMANCE.md Part 2),
    PREDICTED from calls. MEASURED on MartyPC's modelled platter (GLaBIOS,
    which turns a call round faster than the IBM ROM), peek + read: Note Pad
    1,193 -> 1,038 ms, Paint 1,847 -> 1,541, TexPad 1,292 -> 1,097.
    
    Bytes: +206 of .cold and +2 of .text (the hint: a byte in a word, so .text
    after it keeps an even shift) on kern_big and kern_small, one of the
    .cold bytes a never-executed parity pad in the loader. Not on kern_dos
    (its image has no room) nor kern_mega (its store above 1MB lands through a
    nine-sector bounce): DSK_RAHINT is undefined there and both are
    byte-identical. Correctness: every package above opens and runs, and its
    stream must decode to its exact declared length or the loader refuses it.
    Rows: lzload, lzship, disk, filetest, launch (tools/os88hot.py).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
